alidate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2d3d95e4-7576-55a1-aad6-1db486808546" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "9b0099fa-c260-5522-8349-b84319f3d9a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "314ee618-c0ac-565f-8046-5e30b17e6a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "38375f01-3694-5244-ab9b-45e80378100b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "9e00beba-7ccb-5dcd-a645-6ac3f82084ab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "118e46f1-be4c-5208-998c-6bd38711ed4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337765/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-337765/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-337765/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-337765/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-337765/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-337765/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337765" :question/id #uuid "42f52e33-d273-52b4-89f9-837138729e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-337765" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=(x-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)=4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy$" :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=x-1$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=2x.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=4,{f}_{2}(x)=0,{f}_{1}(x)=-{x}^{2},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337765/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337765"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "8a98b0d4-db57-58c0-8523-402735c11fb8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "000ab1f1-7d5c-5a95-813b-e7fb90e63cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f7e40115-e366-5fd4-9457-afe4d83d5af5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "cc815b64-636a-5055-9cf9-3a25a9493747" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b1e136a9-f8b4-5f39-a1a1-b19aaec76d00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "25ab82cd-1aa9-517a-9c8e-e69c0b654c96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337778/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-337778/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-337778/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-337778/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-337778/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-337778/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337778" :question/id #uuid "ae970c05-8468-553f-965f-7819d89308c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-337778" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\n- ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,y$\n- ${D}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y$\n- ${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,y$" :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x},{f}_{1}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-2.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=2,{f}_{2}(x)={e}^{x},{f}_{1}(x)=0,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-337778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "8995a31d-bd20-5ffe-a31c-459c3295c4b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "92d4f52f-fb16-50dd-b967-ddb1d1580aeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "9f0e5ad3-9790-5341-aafa-3f8153ac9a2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "cb7beb16-c2d7-50c0-900e-a455b82ed4eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "2371e7fb-d44f-5656-b5ed-6ed804253cf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1e0702c-75a2-5b2d-b62d-d9738c350e8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64900/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-64900/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-64900/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-64900/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-64900/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-64900/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64900" :question/id #uuid "7e2de42e-6e49-52a4-9c7d-88b4b8bf3ab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-64900" :question/problem "Suppose that $L$ is a linear differential operator such that $L({y}_{1})=2{cos}^{2}⁡x$ and $L({y}_{2})={sin}^{2}⁡x+4$ for some functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ What is $L({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})?$" :question/worked-solution "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nL(a{y}_{1}(x)+b{y}_{2}(x))=aL({y}_{1}(x))+bL({y}_{2}(x))\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2}) & =L({y}_{1})+2L({y}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+2\\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡x+4) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡x+2{sin}^{2}⁡x+8 \\\\  & =2({cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x)+8 \\\\  & =2+8 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-64900/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68148c93-9139-5deb-8a53-a05d63ec5930"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64900"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130076/selection/4fb17f261e904acf135ebcd64b2c6ee5d6d28610997d2d0c2fbe0ff4712d8f99" :answer/id #uuid "de1bc3e8-11cc-570b-a70a-a1ec0620d5ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130076/selection/d5ccc67a0af7ed709899adf357dd9d87e71344eb5b1aa1680a11724ea1238f78" :answer/id #uuid "a5b70014-fbb2-5647-8fa8-99e70d5c049f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130076/selection/6c24ebe4bf973f0938fdfbd36c15af68fcd2bb30b80fbae06180f739fb0d5dce" :answer/id #uuid "f2e1266b-774f-51ad-b38c-cc1ab5fb913d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130076/selection/5fff3fb42090140bbc1f149c168fe1a8e1084bbc815ce806938accfe76e3d0b2" :answer/id #uuid "ec8fbd9a-4410-59c2-a62d-acf93aab0fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/ma